</span>
</div>
</div>
</details>
<details class="recipe" id="recipe-1" data-search="mini wisconsin hot beef sundaes warm-up / pregame 1 lb yukon gold potatoes, peeled and cut into chunks 2 tbsp butter 1/4 cup whole milk or half-and-half, warmed 1/3 tsp kosher salt, plus more to taste 8 oz shaved or very thinly sliced roast beef 1 tbsp butter 1/2 small yellow onion, thinly sliced 1 tbsp flour 1 cup beef broth 1 tsp worcestershire sauce 1/2 tsp dijon mustard black pepper to taste 1/2 cup shredded sharp cheddar 1/3 cup crispy fried onions">
<summary>
<div>
<div class="r-title">Mini Wisconsin Hot Beef Sundaes</div>
<div class="r-mini">
<span class="pill">⏱ 55 minutes</span>
<span class="pill">Moderate</span>
</div>
</div>
<span class="open-label">Open recipe</span>
</summary>
<div class="recipe-body">
<div class="meta-grid">
<div class="meta-card">
<span>Serves</span>3 people • 6 appetizer cups</div>
<div class="meta-card">
<span>Total time</span>55 minutes</div>
<div class="meta-card">
<span>Difficulty</span>Moderate</div>
<div class="meta-card">
<span>Equipment</span>Saucepan; skillet; 6 small ramekins, espresso cups, or sturdy appetizer cups.</div>
</div>
<div class="makeahead">
<b>Make-ahead:</b> Make the mashed potatoes, beef and gravy earlier in the day. Reheat separately and assemble right before serving.</div>
<div class="cols">
<div>
<h3 class="sub">Ingredients</h3>
<ul>
<li>1 lb Yukon Gold potatoes, peeled and cut into chunks</li>
<li>2 tbsp butter</li>
<li>1/4 cup whole milk or half-and-half, warmed</li>
<li>1/3 tsp kosher salt, plus more to taste</li>
<li>8 oz shaved or very thinly sliced roast beef</li>
<li>1 tbsp butter</li>
<li>1/2 small yellow onion, thinly sliced</li>
<li>1 tbsp flour</li>
<li>1 cup beef broth</li>
<li>1 tsp Worcestershire sauce</li>
<li>1/2 tsp Dijon mustard</li>
<li>Black pepper to taste</li>
<li>1/2 cup shredded sharp cheddar</li>
<li>1/3 cup crispy fried onions</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div>
<h3 class="sub">Step-by-step</h3>
<ol>
<li>Put the potatoes in a saucepan, cover with cold salted water and bring to a boil. Reduce to a steady simmer and cook 12–15 minutes, until completely tender.</li>
<li>Drain well, return the potatoes to the warm pan for 1 minute to steam off excess moisture, then mash with butter, warm milk and salt. Keep warm.</li>
<li>Meanwhile, melt 1 tablespoon butter in a skillet over medium heat. Add onion and cook 8–10 minutes until soft and golden.</li>
<li>Sprinkle flour over the onion and stir for 1 minute. Slowly whisk in beef broth, then add Worcestershire and Dijon. Simmer 4–6 minutes until a spoon dragged through the gravy leaves a brief trail.</li>
<li>Tear or chop the roast beef into bite-size pieces and stir it into the gravy just long enough to heat through. Do not boil it aggressively or the beef can toughen.</li>
<li>Spoon about 1/3 cup mashed potatoes into each small serving cup. Make a little dip in the center.</li>
<li>Top each with beef and gravy, then cheddar and crispy onions. Serve warm with small forks.</li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note">
<b>KaySo note:</b> These are intentionally small. The goal is a ridiculous two- or three-bite appetizer, not six bowls of mashed potatoes before dinner.</div>
<div class="actions">
<button class="share" data-share="1">↗ Share Recipe</button>
<button data-copy="1">Copy Recipe</button>
<span id="status-1" class="status">
</span>
</div>
</div>
</details>
<details class="recipe" id="recipe-2" data-search="smoked buffalo chicken pinwheels warm-up / pregame 1 sheet frozen puff pastry, thawed but still cold 1 cup cooked shredded chicken 1/3 cup buffalo sauce 3 oz cream cheese, softened 3/4 cup shredded sharp cheddar 2 scallions, thinly sliced 1/2 tsp ranch seasoning 1 egg beaten with 1 tsp water ranch dressing, for serving">
<summary>
<div>
<div class="r-title">Smoked Buffalo Chicken Pinwheels</div>
<div class="r-mini">
<span class="pill">⏱ 50 minutes</span>
<span class="pill">Easy</span>
</div>
</div>
<span class="open-label">Open recipe</span>
</summary>
<div class="recipe-body">
<div class="meta-grid">
<div class="meta-card">
<span>Serves</span>3 people • 12 pinwheels</div>
<div class="meta-card">
<span>Total time</span>50 minutes</div>
<div class="meta-card">
<span>Difficulty</span>Easy</div>
<div class="meta-card">
<span>Equipment</span>Sheet pan; parchment; smoker or oven.</div>
</div>
<div class="makeahead">
<b>Make-ahead:</b> Mix the filling and roll the pastry up to 6 hours ahead. Chill, then slice and bake/smoke when needed.</div>
<div class="cols">
<div>
<h3 class="sub">Ingredients</h3>
<ul>
<li>1 sheet frozen puff pastry, thawed but still cold</li>
<li>1 cup cooked shredded chicken</li>
<li>1/3 cup buffalo sauce</li>
<li>3 oz cream cheese, softened</li>
<li>3/4 cup shredded sharp cheddar</li>
<li>2 scallions, thinly sliced</li>
<li>1/2 tsp ranch seasoning</li>
<li>1 egg beaten with 1 tsp water</li>
<li>Ranch dressing, for serving</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div>
<h3 class="sub">Step-by-step</h3>
<ol>
<li>Heat the oven or smoker to 400°F. If using the smoker, make sure it is running clean smoke; puff pastry picks up smoke quickly.</li>
<li>Mix chicken, buffalo sauce, cream cheese, cheddar, scallions and ranch seasoning until evenly combined.</li>
<li>Unfold the puff pastry on a lightly floured surface. Gently roll it into roughly a 10x12-inch rectangle.</li>
<li>Spread the chicken filling over the pastry, leaving a 1/2-inch border along one long edge.</li>
<li>Starting from the opposite long edge, roll tightly into a log. Chill 10 minutes if the pastry has become soft.</li>
<li>Slice into 12 equal rounds with a sharp knife. Arrange cut-side up on parchment and brush the exposed pastry lightly with egg wash.</li>
<li>Bake or smoke 18–23 minutes, rotating the pan once, until deeply golden and crisp.</li>
<li>Rest 5 minutes before serving. Put ranch on the side rather than drenching the pinwheels so the pastry stays crisp.</li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note">
<b>KaySo note:</b> If your smoker struggles to stay at 400°F, smoke them at 325°F for about 10 minutes for flavor, then finish in a 425°F oven until crisp.</div>
<div class="actions">
<button class="share" data-share="2">↗ Share Recipe</button>
<button data-copy="2">Copy Recipe</button>
<span id="status-2" class="status">
</span>
</div>
</div>
</details>
<details class="recipe" id="recipe-3" data-search="mini loaded potato cups warm-up / pregame 12 small baby yukon gold or red potatoes, about 1 1/2 inches wide 1 tbsp olive oil 3/4 tsp kosher salt, divided 1/2 tsp black pepper 4 slices bacon, cooked crisp and chopped 3/4 cup shredded sharp cheddar 1/3 cup sour cream 2 scallions, thinly sliced 1/4 tsp smoked paprika">
<summary>
<div>
<div class="r-title">Mini Loaded Potato Cups</div>
<div class="r-mini">
<span class="pill">⏱ 55 minutes</span>
<span class="pill">Easy</span>
</div>
</div>
<span class="open-label">Open recipe</span>
</summary>
<div class="recipe-body">
<div class="meta-grid">
<div class="meta-card">
<span>Serves</span>3 people • 12 potato cups</div>
<div class="meta-card">
<span>Total time</span>55 minutes</div>
<div class="meta-card">
<span>Difficulty</span>Easy</div>
<div class="meta-card">
<span>Equipment</span>Sheet pan; small spoon or melon baller.</div>
</div>
<div class="makeahead">
<b>Make-ahead:</b> Roast and scoop the potatoes a few hours ahead. Fill and finish just before serving.</div>
<div class="cols">
<div>
<h3 class="sub">Ingredients</h3>
<ul>
<li>12 small baby Yukon Gold or red potatoes, about 1 1/2 inches wide</li>
<li>1 tbsp olive oil</li>
<li>3/4 tsp kosher salt, divided</li>
<li>1/2 tsp black pepper</li>
<li>4 slices bacon, cooked crisp and chopped</li>
<li>3/4 cup shredded sharp cheddar</li>
<li>1/3 cup sour cream</li>
<li>2 scallions, thinly sliced</li>
<li>1/4 tsp smoked paprika</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div>
<h3 class="sub">Step-by-step</h3>
<ol>
<li>Heat oven to 425°F. Toss potatoes with oil, 1/2 teaspoon salt and pepper. Roast 25–30 minutes until tender.</li>
<li>Cool until you can handle them, then halve each potato lengthwise.</li>
<li>Use a small spoon to scoop a shallow well from each half. Leave enough potato around the skin so the cups do not collapse.</li>
<li>Arrange cut-side up on the sheet pan and return to the oven for 8–10 minutes so the edges dry and crisp.</li>
<li>Mix cheddar, bacon and about half the scallions. Spoon a small mound into each potato cup.</li>
<li>Bake another 5–7 minutes until the cheese is melted and bubbling.</li>
<li>Stir sour cream with the remaining 1/4 teaspoon salt and smoked paprika. Add a tiny dollop to each potato and finish with the remaining scallions.</li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note">
<b>KaySo note:</b> Do not overfill these. They are better as crisp little potato shells with a concentrated topping than as miniature twice-baked potatoes.</div>
<div class="actions">
<button class="share" data-share="3">↗ Share Recipe</button>
<button data-copy="3">Copy Recipe</button>
<span id="status-3" class="status">
</span>
</div>
</div>
</details>
<details class="recipe" id="recipe-4" data-search="bloody mary steak bites warm-up / pregame 12 oz sirloin steak, cut into 1-inch cubes 1 tbsp neutral oil 1 tsp worcestershire sauce 3/4 tsp celery salt 1/2 tsp coarse black pepper 1/4 tsp onion powder pinch of cayenne, optional 1 tbsp butter 1/3 cup sour cream 2 tbsp mayonnaise 1 1/2 tbsp prepared horseradish 1 tsp dijon mustard 1 tsp worcestershire sauce black pepper to taste">
<summary>
<div>
<div class="r-title">Bloody Mary Steak Bites</div>
<div class="r-mini">
<span class="pill">⏱ 30 minutes</span>
<span class="pill">Moderate</span>
</div>
</div>
<span class="open-label">Open recipe</span>
</summary>
<div class="recipe-body">
<div class="meta-grid">
<div class="meta-card">
<span>Serves</span>3 people • appetizer portion</div>
<div class="meta-card">
<span>Total time</span>30 minutes</div>
<div class="meta-card">
<span>Difficulty</span>Moderate</div>
<div class="meta-card">
<span>Equipment</span>Heavy skillet or griddle; tongs.</div>
</div>
<div class="makeahead">
<b>Make-ahead:</b> Make the horseradish sauce a day ahead. Cut and season the steak up to 2 hours ahead.</div>
<div class="cols">
<div>
<h3 class="sub">Ingredients</h3>
<ul>
<li>12 oz sirloin steak, cut into 1-inch cubes</li>
<li>1 tbsp neutral oil</li>
<li>1 tsp Worcestershire sauce</li>
<li>3/4 tsp celery salt</li>
<li>1/2 tsp coarse black pepper</li>
<li>1/4 tsp onion powder</li>
<li>Pinch of cayenne, optional</li>
<li>1 tbsp butter</li>
<li>1/3 cup sour cream</li>
<li>2 tbsp mayonnaise</li>
<li>1 1/2 tbsp prepared horseradish</li>
<li>1 tsp Dijon mustard</li>
<li>1 tsp Worcestershire sauce</li>
<li>Black pepper to taste</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div>
<h3 class="sub">Step-by-step</h3>
<ol>
<li>Mix sour cream, mayo, horseradish, Dijon, Worcestershire and pepper. Refrigerate while you cook the steak.</li>
<li>Pat the steak cubes very dry. Toss with oil, Worcestershire, celery salt, black pepper, onion powder and cayenne.</li>
<li>Heat a heavy skillet over high heat until very hot. Work in two batches if necessary so the steak sears instead of steaming.</li>
<li>Add steak in a single layer and leave it alone for 60–90 seconds. Turn and cook another 60–90 seconds for medium-rare to medium, depending on cube size.</li>
<li>Add butter for the final 30 seconds and toss the steak through it.</li>
<li>Transfer immediately to a platter. Let rest 3 minutes, then serve with toothpicks and the cold horseradish sauce.</li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note">
